        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` runs a tiny repo task twice. First as prompt only, then with the seven surfaces wired in. Same model, same task. The script counts which surfaces were missing on the failed run and prints a failure-mode report."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The repo task is small on purpose: add input validation to a one-file FastAPI-style handler and write a passing test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: a side-by-side log of the two runs, a `failure_modes.json` summarizing the prompt-only run, and a one-line verdict for the workbench run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The agent is a tiny rule-based stub; the point is the surfaces, not the model. Across the rest of this mini-track you will rebuild each surface as a real, reusable artifact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Pick a repo where you already run an agent. Score the seven surfaces from 0 (missing) to 2 (healthy). What is your weakest surface?\n2. Extend `main.py` so the prompt-only run also produces a fake \"success\" claim. Verify the verification gate would have caught it.\n3. Add an eighth surface for your own product. Justify why it does not collapse into one of the existing seven.\n4. Re-run the script with a different stub agent that hallucinates an extra file write. Which surface catches it first?\n5. Map the five industry-recurring failure modes from Phase 14 \u00b7 26 onto the seven surfaces. Which mode is each surface designed to absorb?"
      ]
    }
